## How to blend them on this project

- **Stack reality**: Rust workspace (`crates/`) — RDP server (`macrdp-server`), capture, input, encode, clipboard, audio — on **IronRDP forks** (`ironrdp-server-gfx`, `ironrdp-acceptor-patched`). Desktop shell: **Tauri 2 + React/Vite** (`macrdp-ui/`). Target **macOS 14+** only; respect Screen Recording and Accessibility permissions. Do not claim Windows/Linux server support unless code implements it.
- **Architecture** (Software Architect lens): Keep crate boundaries clear (protocol vs capture vs encode vs platform I/O). Prefer changes upstream in IronRDP when possible; document why local patches exist. Name trade-offs for latency, bitrate, AVC420 vs AVC444, hardware vs software encode, and lock-screen capture paths.
- **Rust / protocol** (Backend Architect lens): Async Tokio, structured errors (`anyhow` / explicit types where it helps API stability), `tracing` for observability. Touch patched IronRDP crates carefully — run `cargo build` / targeted tests after protocol changes. GPL v3 applies to distribution; respect license when borrowing from FreeRDP/RustDesk references.
- **macOS native** (Backend + Security lenses): VideoToolbox, CoreGraphics, pasteboard, and input injection must fail safely with actionable logs. Never weaken NLA/CredSSP or TLS defaults for convenience; treat default `config.example.toml` credentials as demo-only.
- **Frontend** (Frontend Developer lens): Tauri commands as the IPC boundary; no secrets in the webview storage. Accessible controls (Radix/Base UI patterns already in tree), honest connection/metrics UI (no fabricated stats). Match existing pages: Dashboard, Settings, Permissions, Statistics, Logs.
- **DevOps** (DevOps Automator lens): `Makefile`, `macrdp-ui/build.sh`, `.github/workflows/release.yml`, and codesign/bundle scripts must stay aligned with actual artifacts. Config search paths: `./config.toml`, `~/.config/macrdp/`, `~/Library/Application Support/macrdp/`.
- **Documentation** (Technical Writer lens): User-visible or config changes update `README.md` and `config.example.toml` when behavior differs from `docs/`. Commands in README must build on macOS 14+ with Rust 1.75+.
- **Reviews**: Self-check with 🔴 blocker / 🟡 suggestion / 💭 nit before finishing non-trivial changes (especially security, encoding, and IronRDP patches).

